                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A survive-the-night game that requires you to learn the mechanics of each character if you want to make it through each hour before your escape. I had this in my wishlist for a while, not sure what to expect and maybe had I played this years ago I might have felt different but it is really rough. For starters it’s not actually clear when the gameplay starts. There’s also some sort of active issue where encountering a character in the start of the game causes the game to crash consistently. You don’t have to trigger them then but it is a problem nonetheless.  You wander around a bunch looking for clues figuring out where to start but it’s unknowingly a matter of waiting. In fact, a lot of this game is waiting. Not in the, survive sort of way but even waiting for a character to do something waiting. Like, the hours feel so long and you have to do so little in them especially once you know each character's trick. There were times that even when adhering to the rules of each character a glitch or something would cause them to break that rule and kill you anyways. Rare, but it happened more than once with varying characters. Otherwise it’s super easy… until you get to the final hour in which the game can block you out of winning. By this I mean that depending on spawns and combinations, characters can stop you from finishing an objective in time (even at times physically blocking you). So, there’s a bit of RNG involved especially when I have had a character spawn on top of me. Luckily, you get checkpoints every hour even if you die so you don’t have to suffer through the time it takes to get to that point.\n",
